From 4cd11b121ecb32e9375b2895073fe721c0424c38 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "suricata.lu" <suricata.lu@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:39:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: j721e: pass PD_FLAG_* to dev_pm_domain_attach()

CIP patch 0819 (upstream d42c7c6fd66a "PM: domains: Add flags to specify
power on attach/detach") changed the second argument of
dev_pm_domain_attach() from "bool power_on" to a u32 flag mask and
converted all upstream callers. TI's 7669c931b19e ("FROMLIST: PCI: j721e:
Fix programming sequence of "strap" settings") adds a caller that is not
upstream, so it still passes "true", which now means PD_FLAG_NO_DEV_LINK.

Pass PD_FLAG_ATTACH_POWER_ON as 0819 does for the other callers, and
PD_FLAG_DETACH_POWER_OFF so that the re-attach uses the same flags as
platform_probe(), which attached the domain that j721e_pcie_probe()
detaches before programming the strap settings.

On a DT system genpd_dev_pm_attach() always powers on the domain and
PD_FLAG_NO_DEV_LINK is not used by dev_pm_domain_attach(), and
detach_power_off is only used on the Renesas RZ machines listed in
dev_pm_domain_allow_detach_on_unbind_cleanup(), so there is no change in
behaviour on TI K3; this keeps the meaning of the call correct.
---
 drivers/pci/controller/cadence/pci-j721e.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/cadence/pci-j721e.c b/drivers/pci/controller/cadence/pci-j721e.c
index 7a70c085eb83..92a58d0565dd 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/cadence/pci-j721e.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/cadence/pci-j721e.c
@@ -495,7 +495,8 @@ static int j721e_pcie_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
 
-	ret = dev_pm_domain_attach(dev, true);
+	ret = dev_pm_domain_attach(dev, PD_FLAG_ATTACH_POWER_ON |
+					 PD_FLAG_DETACH_POWER_OFF);
 	if (ret < 0) {
 		dev_err(dev, "failed to power on PCIe Controller\n");
 		return ret;
